14	// The tests of the upstream lifecycle (DEVDESK-505, NX-02a, step 5):
15	//
16	//	ReadUpstream(ctx, runner, p) (UpstreamState, error)
17	//	EnsureUpstream(ctx, runner, clock, p, out) error
18	//
19	// against the scripted kubectl of preflight_test.go, wrapped by upstreamKubectl
20	// below, and the fake clock of clock_test.go. No real kubectl, no real wait.
21	//
22	// Neither function runs a preflight: the callers do (Deploy, then seed). The
23	// kubectl calls the tests assume (arguments after "kubectl", without --context;
24	// "--request-timeout=<d>" may sit anywhere and is ignored):
25	//
26	//	get deployment[s] [bench-upstream | deployment/bench-upstream] -n <ns> -o json
27	//	                          one object when named, a list when not (it then holds
28	//	                          the Deployment of Nexus too: the reader picks by name)
29	//	get pods -n <ns> -l app.kubernetes.io/name=bench-upstream -o json
30	//	get pvc [bench-upstream-data] -n <ns> [-l <selector>] -o json
31	//	                          the list holds the claim of Nexus too, listed first
32	//	scale deployment/bench-upstream --replicas=1 -n <ns>   (or "deployment bench-upstream")
33	//
34	// Choices of the tests, to settle with the code:
35	//   - ReadUpstream: absent Deployment is Missing; zero replicas is Cut (even while
36	//     an old pod is still terminating); one replica without a ready pod that is
37	//     not terminating is Starting (a pod that fails to pull is Starting, not an
38	//     error: diagnosing is the wait's job); a ready pod that is not terminating
39	//     is Ready. It writes nothing and waits for nothing.
40	//   - EnsureUpstream reads first. Cut: exactly one write, the scale to 1, then
41	//     the wait. Starting: no write, the wait. Ready: no write, no wait, nil.
42	//     Missing: an error, no write (Deploy applies the Deployment before).
43	//   - The wait reads the pods and the claim of the UPSTREAM only (selector
44	//     app.kubernetes.io/name=bench-upstream, claim bench-upstream-data), once per
45	//     round, diagnoses, then sleeps between 1 s and 10 s; it gives up at
46	//     p.Timeout (within one interval) with a Deadline that cites the pod.
47	//   - Its messages name NEXUS_BENCH_UPSTREAM_IMAGE and _TAG for a pull failure,
48	//     and never the variables that size Nexus (the upstream is not sized by
49	//     them) nor "the Nexus pod".
50	//   - A custom upstream URL is refused before any call, with a message that
51	//     names NEXUS_BENCH_UPSTREAM_URL.
52	//   - A cancelled context is returned as is.
53	
54	const (
55		// upstreamName is declared by render_test.go ("bench-upstream").
56		upstreamClaim    = "bench-upstream-data"
57		upstreamSelector = "app.kubernetes.io/name=bench-upstream"
58		upstreamPodName  = "REDACTED"
59	)
